## Summary

Shipped the production-grade native Apple `VersionInfoWidget` surface — a faithful SwiftUI parity of `features/dashboard/widgets/VersionInfoWidget.tsx` — as a 7-file bundle in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/`, mirroring the accepted `UptimeMonitorWidget` precedent. Committed as `8a9a0bfc1` (8 files incl. log, 1745 insertions).

**What was built**
- `.Projection.swift` — Foundation-only adapter: DTOs, `VersionInfoProjector` (verbatim port of `?? '—'` fallbacks, `gitSha.slice(0,7)`, two-decimal GB `formatBytes`), locale-aware formatters, i18n facade, testable a11y summary.
- `.Model.swift` — P1/S8 state-holder (`@Observable`, phase resolution, `isCompact ≤1`/`isWide ≥4`), P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, registry (`version-info`, system, 2×2/1×2/4×40 + clamp).
- `.Components.swift` / `.swift` — token-styled subviews + responsive compact/standard/wide layouts rendering **every** state (loading/empty/error/content + stale/offline freshness); no networking in the view.
- `.Previews.swift` (8 states), `.Tests.swift` (25 cases), `.strings` (all 13 web keys + chrome).

**Verification (real Xcode 26.5 toolchain via `DEVELOPER_DIR`)**
- swiftlint --strict: **0 violations** · swiftformat --lint: **0** · placeholder: **0** (scanner self-test passes)
- adapter host-harness **executed 24/24** · full XCTest suite **executed 25/25** (SwiftPM, Swift 6 strict-concurrency)
